Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-16-2001||12:19 PM||||I have an 85, 4cyl, 5spd, and I was driving home from Toronto yesterday (never driven the car that far before.. like 1.5 hours each way), and I was doing about 140-150 for a while, and ten I had to slow down, and almost come to a complete stop. It was IMPOSSIBLE to get it into any gears! I finally had to shut the car off, and put it in first, and then later, i realized it was working fine. And then a bit later, same problems. Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||03-16-2001||01:44 PM||||Nevermind. today I had to stop and start in first gear a bunch of times. Seems to happen every few times I stop. The pedal feels spongier, doesn't require as much effort, and the car seems to move when I let the clutch go even .5mm from the floor. Fluid is still at full, lines are new, clutch is new, agh! Master and slave look good! I need clutch wire!||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||03-16-2001||02:30 PM||||What if I were to fabriate a loogner slave pushrod? Or move the whole slave cylinder closer to the clutch arm?||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||03-16-2001||02:50 PM||||Other theory. fabricate new slave bracket, so it mounts closer to the transmission, thereby hitting a lower point on the clutch arm, and making more throw... good idea?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||03-16-2001||03:34 PM||||Try this, jack up the left rear of the car high enough that the slave is level or bleeder valve end higher than level. Then bleed the system, one push should be enough. Sounds as if there is a small pocket of air trapped inside the slave cylinder!||||reg||1
